          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/velocity"} velocity
            for rotational movement.
          %p
            For rotation in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            inside a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            the angular velocity is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivector"} bivector
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^2 \mathbb{R}^n
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ˙
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\dot \omega \,\, e_1 \wedge e_2
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_2
            are unit vector spanning the plane of rotation, and where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ˙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dot \omega
            is the magnitude of the angular velocity.
          %p
            Of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
            (and only then) can we identify
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivector"} bivector
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector"} vector
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge star operator
